<title>USA: MedCare expands into Florida.</title>
<headline>MedCare expands into Florida.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>MedCare Technologies Inc said Friday it opened its third urinary incontinence treatment center, in Winter Park, Fla., in conjunction with Urology Consultants.</p>
<p>It said its entry into the Florida market with the first of five sites, along with currently operating centers serving Oklahoma City and Kansas City, continue to mark MedCare's transition from a development stage company.</p>
<p>It is becoming a commercial vendor of non-surgical and non-drug medical protocol for treating urinary incontinence.</p>
<p>MedCare said centers also are planned for Illinois, Texas, Colorado, Arizona, California and New York.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
